  "notes": "WATCH OUT:\nNot to be confused with the homophone {電波|でんぱ} (radio waves). Different kanji, different meaning.\n\nREGISTER:\nFormal and academic. Used in written contexts — scholarly articles, news reports, medical literature. In casual speech, {広|ひろ}がる or {広|ひろ}まる is more natural.\n\nUSAGE:\n- {感染症|かんせんしょう}の{伝播|でんぱ}: spread of infectious disease\n- {文化|ぶんか}の{伝播|でんぱ}: cultural transmission\n- {情報|じょうほう}の{伝播|でんぱ}: spread of information\n- {音|おと}の{伝播|でんぱ}: propagation of sound (physics)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {急速|きゅうそく}に{伝播|でんぱ}する: to spread rapidly\n- 〜を{通|つう}じて{伝播|でんぱ}する: to spread through/via 〜\n\nPRONUNCIATION:\nThe standard reading is でんぱ. The alternative reading でんぱん is occasionally seen but less common.",
